    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Breakfast Enchiladas Recipe",
      "description": "We’ve been posting quite a few enchilada recipes lately, and what can I say, it’s just one of my favorite dishes to eat. This style replaces the tortillas with eggs, and the meat with sausage, creating a great breakfast option. Everything is topped with enchilada sauce and cheddar cheese.\n\n*Don’t forget to check the labels for the enchilada sauce when you’re at the store. Mostly will only have a few carbs, but there are some brands that have added sugars or thickeners.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n\nTortillas\n6 large eggs\n¼ cup heavy whipping cream\n½ teaspoon salt\n½ teaspoon garlic powder\n½ teaspoon chili powder\n¼ teaspoon black pepper\n\nEnchiladas\n8 ounces ground sausage\n¾ cup enchilada sauce\n1½ cups shredded cheddar cheese\n\nNutrition Summary:\nThis makes a total of 4 servings of Keto Breakfast Enchiladas. Each serving comes out to be 524.5 Calories, 42.55g Fats, 6.08g Net Carbs, and 27.3g Protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14-day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
